---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "35 × 45 mm Passport Photo Sheet — Free A4 Print Tool";
const description = "Make a 35 × 45 mm passport photo sheet for A4 printing. Compare PDF and JPEG outputs, see an illustrated example, and open Chintan Puggalok's free browser tool.";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <main class="page-shell">
    <header class="page-hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">Free browser tool · Indian passport-style photo</p>
      <h1>Make a 35 × 45 mm passport photo sheet on A4</h1>
      <p>Prepare a 35 × 45 mm portrait, arrange multiple copies on A4, and download a PDF or JPEG for printing. No image editor required.</p>
      <p><a class="button button-primary" href="https://create-passport-photo.chintanpuggalok.com/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Open the free photo maker <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p>
    </header>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="steps-heading">
      <h2 id="steps-heading">How to make your photo sheet</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Choose a clear, recent portrait from your device.</li>
        <li>Position and crop the photo in the editor; review the framing yourself.</li>
        <li>Download the A4 PDF or JPEG and print at 100% / Actual size.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>Check the instructions for your specific passport application before printing. Requirements can vary by application and authority.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="example-heading">
      <h2 id="example-heading">See the photo-to-sheet workflow</h2>
      <figure>
        <img src="https://create-passport-photo.chintanpuggalok.com/demo-showcase.jpg" width="960" height="480" loading="lazy" decoding="async" style="display:block;max-width:100%;height:auto" alt="Synthetic portrait, white-background crop, and an A4 print sheet of 30 copies" />
        <figcaption>Original illustration → white-background crop → A4 sheet. This is a synthetic workflow illustration, not proof of AI quality or official acceptance.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <p><a href="https://create-passport-photo.chintanpuggalok.com/demo-portrait.jpg">View the small demo JPG (9 KB)</a>. No real person's photo is used.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="outputs-heading">
      <h2 id="outputs-heading">Choose the right download and print settings</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Single-photo JPEG:</strong> one cropped image at 300 DPI. A print JPEG does not automatically meet an online portal's pixel dimensions or file-size limits.</li>
        <li><strong>A4 PDF:</strong> a sheet containing multiple copies, ready to save or hand to a print service.</li>
        <li><strong>A4 JPEG:</strong> the same arranged sheet as an image, not an individual photo.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>The default 35 × 45 mm photos, 5 mm page margin and 3 mm gaps fit 30 copies: 5 columns × 6 rows. Custom dimensions, margins and gaps change the count.</p>
      <p>Print on A4 at <strong>Actual size / 100%</strong>, with Fit to page and automatic shrinking turned off. Measure a sample with a ruler before printing a batch: the printer or service can override your settings.</p>
      <p>The tool works with common phone-image formats and local HEIC/HEIF conversion; AVIF depends on the browser. Editing and downloads are free, with no account or watermark. Contributions are optional.</p>
      <p>Read the <a href="/writing/building-a-private-indian-passport-photo-tool/#photo-sizing-and-printing">photo sizing and A4 printing section</a> of the original build article for the full guide.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="privacy-heading">
      <h2 id="privacy-heading">Your photo stays in your browser</h2>
      <p>Photo editing and export happen locally in your browser. The app's server does not receive your portrait or exported PDF. Drafts may be saved in browser storage on your device; clear saved photos before sharing a device.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="limits-heading">
      <h2 id="limits-heading">A preparation tool, not an official validator</h2>
      <p>The tool helps crop a portrait and prepare a print layout. It cannot confirm that a photo meets every official requirement or will be accepted. Follow the latest <a href="https://www.passportindia.gov.in/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Passport Seva guidance</a> for your application.</p>
      <p>Read the complete <a href="/writing/building-a-private-indian-passport-photo-tool/">passport photo maker build story</a>, including <a href="/writing/building-a-private-indian-passport-photo-tool/#photo-sizing-and-printing">photo sizing and A4 printing</a>, browser privacy, storage, and testing decisions.</p>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
